      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:33:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The email field is split only on commas, so `John Doe \u003cjohn@ifonica.example\u003e` never matches and that subscriber gets a 404. PortaBilling\u0027s own email lookup for password reset accepts both forms: `(^|,)\\s*ADDR\\s*(,|$)` or `\u003c\\s*ADDR\\s*\u003e` (`Porta/PasswordsRole.pm`, `$_EMAIL_REGEXP_FMT`). Please use the same rule here: take the address from inside `\u003c…\u003e` when it is there, then compare it without case. Please also add a test for that form.\n\n**Co-Reviewed By: deep-code-reviewer**",
      "revId": "96cdb4aa96a101216a8666edbdab12405d2e9ea6",
      "serverId": "b3d83be1-eb64-49fe-9bf1-b81a817d2fd2"
    },
