      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:33:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`OTP_LOGIN_IDENTIFIERS` still advertises only `(\u0027phone_number\u0027,)`, and `/system-info` hands this to the clients (`main.py:490`). The mobile app picks its sign-in UI from it (`otp_signin_identifier.dart`): with phone only it shows \"Enter your phone number\", a text keyboard, phone autofill and the phone wording for `delivery_channel_unspecified`. The adapter now accepts an email, but Ifonica users will be told to type a phone number, so requirement 1 of WT-2212 is not met end to end.\n\nPlease advertise `(\u0027phone_number\u0027, \u0027email\u0027)`. If showing \"phone or email\" on every PortaSwitch tenant is not wanted, make it a setting. In that case the \"no switch\" note in CLAUDE.md/README needs updating.\n\n**Co-Reviewed By: deep-code-reviewer**",
      "revId": "96cdb4aa96a101216a8666edbdab12405d2e9ea6",
      "serverId": "b3d83be1-eb64-49fe-9bf1-b81a817d2fd2"
    },
    {
