      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:33:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A single `get_account_list` call with `limit\u003d1000` can miss matches. `%john@gmail.com%` also matches `ajohn@gmail.com`, `xjohn@gmail.com.ua`, and so on, so on a large tenant there can be more than 1000 candidates. When the exact matches are past row 1000, the result is either a false 404, or only one match is seen while a second account outside the window has the same address. In the second case a code is sent, which breaks requirement 4 (\"several accounts, no OTP\").\n\n`LIKE \u0027%addr%\u0027` plus the exact post-filter is the right approach. It is how PortaBilling\u0027s own account search behaves (`Porta/Account.pm:10536`), and the field can hold several addresses, so please keep it. Just page through the candidates: pass `get_total: 1` plus `offset` in `find_accounts_by_email`, loop until the rows run out, stop early as soon as a second exact match is found (raise `ambiguous_user_ref`), and refuse above a hard cap (for example 10 000 rows) rather than pick an account from a partial list.\n\nPlease add a test where the candidates span more than one page.\n\n**Co-Reviewed By: deep-code-reviewer**",
      "revId": "96cdb4aa96a101216a8666edbdab12405d2e9ea6",
      "serverId": "b3d83be1-eb64-49fe-9bf1-b81a817d2fd2"
    },
